The code has two distinct bugs — one in parsing, one in the app lifecycle. Let me address both.

Bug 1: Silent typo swallowing

The loop ignores any unrecognized parameter instead of warning the operator. In MOOS-IvP AppCasting style, you should track whether each parameter was handled, then report anything that wasn't:

cpp
bool MyApp::OnStartUp()
{
  bool handled = true;             // accumulates overall success

  list<string> params;
  m_MissionReader.GetConfiguration(GetAppName(), params);

  for (auto line : params) {
    string param = tolower(biteStringX(line, '='));
    string value = line;          // remainder after '='

    if (param == "threshold")
      handled = setPosDoubleOnString(m_threshold, value);
    else
      reportUnhandledConfigWarning(param);  // surfaces in AppCast
  }

  registerVariables();
  return handled;
}

Key fixes:

tolower() on the param name makes matching case-insensitive (standard MOOS-IvP convention)
setPosDoubleOnString() (or setDoubleOnString()) validates the value and returns false on bad input, rather than silently giving atof() a 0
reportUnhandledConfigWarning() pushes the unknown param into the AppCast panel so the operator sees it immediately at startup
handled propagates failure back to the return value, which MOOSDB can surface
Bug 2: Mail never arrives — missing registerVariables()

OnStartUp() is the right place to call registerVariables(), which itself calls Register() for every MOOS variable you care about. Without it, the MOOSDB never knows to forward mail to your app:

cpp
void MyApp::registerVariables()
{
  AppCastingMOOSApp::RegisterVariables();  // registers APPCAST_REQ etc.
  Register("SOME_VAR", 0);
  Register("OTHER_VAR", 0);
}

If registerVariables() is never called from OnStartUp(), OnNewMail() will never fire — the app sits silently starved of messages. This is a very common MOOS-IvP gotcha.

The corrected full pattern
cpp
bool MyApp::OnStartUp()
{
  AppCastingMOOSApp::OnStartUp();   // must call base class first

  bool handled = true;

  list<string> params;
  m_MissionReader.GetConfiguration(GetAppName(), params);

  for (auto line : params) {
    string param = tolower(biteStringX(line, '='));
    string value = line;

    if (param == "threshold")
      handled = handled && setPosDoubleOnString(m_threshold, value);
    else if (param == "appstick_hz")
      handled = handled && setDoubleOnString(m_hz, value);
    else
      reportUnhandledConfigWarning(param);
  }

  registerVariables();
  return handled;
}

Three conceptual rules to remember for any MOOS-IvP app:

Always call the base class AppCastingMOOSApp::OnStartUp() first
Always call registerVariables() at the end of OnStartUp() — not in the constructor, not lazily
Every unrecognized param gets reportUnhandledConfigWarning() — never silently drop it

